<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Every string a person reads on Android, in the source language.

    The seven `values-*/strings.xml` beside this one carry the same ids, and
    they are complete: there is no `tools:ignore="MissingTranslation"` left in
    this file and none should come back. Android *does* fall back to this file
    for a key a language is missing — which is exactly why the suppression is
    dangerous rather than harmless, since the fall-back is silent and looks
    like a working screen with one English word in it.

    Two kinds of string are deliberately not here. A `ClipData` label is a
    debugging aid the system clipboard editor shows and no part of Koru draws.
    A language's own name (`Español`, `日本語`) is written in itself in every
    localization — see `SettingsScreen.kt`.
-->
