    <!-- The identity mismatch: the seeds this phone holds no longer produce
         the keys its stored identity names. The content is fine and saying so
         is the point — this state was once mistaken for data loss.

         The explainer is **not** iOS's sentence and must not be made into it.
         Android's `allowBackup="false"` plus an uninstall taking
         `noBackupFilesDir` means a reinstall really is a fresh device here, so
         iOS's "after you reinstall" clause would be a new lie on this
         platform. ADR-413 says so; translate this English, not that one. -->
